{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9113f6895bb3c1522a19b0a14958f15cd80e1e2e30ceb732f73c30274b98611a","digest":{"component_or_area":"Outbound type mapping and per-project skip configuration","key_entities":["mapping_config.MappingLayer","config.effective_type_map","config.assert_type_decisions_complete","config.effective_excluded_sync_types","config.jira_to_local_type","LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA","EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES","rebar-type:","outbound_labels._REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX","outbound_labels._desired_type_annotation","inbound_fields.recover_type_label","outbound_mutation_builders.py","outbound_differ.compute_outbound_mutations","TicketType","mapping_config.SKIP"],"problem_keywords":["type mapping","config-driven","type-granular skip","round-trip safety","rebar-type label","fail-closed","lossy collapse","type resolution"],"propositions":["Config-driven type mapping via MappingLayer.type_map must be threaded through all three OutboundMapper implementations and both field mappers to replace hardcoded LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA, with fail-closed behavior on undecided syncable types before mutation execution","Per-project type exclusion is determined by union of EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES and any local types mapped to SKIP sentinel, replacing the single global EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES at both consumer sites (differ loop and absent-gets selection)","Round-trip type safety requires symmetric rebar-type: annotation labels stamped when type mapping is lossy (distinct local types collapse to one Jira type), using a config-driven reverse map jira_to_local_type, with label-based recovery on inbound","The rebar-type: prefix must be added to all four internal label exclusion tuples across outbound_labels, inbound_collection_diffs, differ, and inbound_translate modules to prevent type annotations from syncing as user tags","Fail-closed type validation must occur once up-front before the mutation loop in compute_outbound_mutations, asserting every syncable local type is decided (mapped to target or SKIP) via assert_type_decisions_complete","acli.create_issue remains unchanged as a passthrough; type resolution occurs only in mapper output paths where issuetype is already set to mapped Jira NAME, not raw local type"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787903823717244001,"uuid":"c24f66b1-f1d6-47f5-b75a-cc25a697a222"}